sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: docs/reference/feature-flow.md section 6, one Swamp workflow per Gateway release, manual or automatic.
  %% A failed check switches back; migrations are expand and contract. docs/reference/gateway-recovery.md#release-as-a-swamp-run.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: gateway:release:deploy
  %% kind: gateway.release
  %% behavior name: gateway-release-<step>-209 (fixed)
  autonumber
  %% lane TR icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane AC icon=workflow pill=child tone=green
  %% lane GN icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant TR as CLI<br/>orbit · MCP
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant AC as Activate run<br/>child · new commit
  participant GN as Gateway Node<br/>Node 14
  alt Recover Swamp after an offline rollback
    TR->>GW: gateway:release:deploy --reconcile<br/>exact serving SHA
    GW->>SW: operation-gateway-reconcile
    SW->>GN: Confirm serving revision and wait for protected Operations
    SW->>SW: Reload retained workflows on Node 209
    SW->>GN: Verify public Gateway and exact live selection
    SW-->>GW: Verified release record
  else Deploy a release
  TR->>GW: gateway:release:deploy<br/>full sha
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit gateway:release:deploy <full sha>`; the automatic tick admits the newest green commit the same way
  Note over GW: Admit the release<br/>verify agent pin · web build
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the full commit; no other release queued or running
  %%> - the agent pin passes its Sigstore check; CI published the commit's web build
  %%> Result:
  %%> - a running release record; the pin, artifact, Horizon unit and SSH targets frozen as inputs
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-gateway-release
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - at run start, mints one read token (contents, actions) into the vault
  GW-->>TR: 202 Accepted<br/>running release record
  SW->>GN: Fetch the commit<br/>shared repository
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - fetches the commit with the read token when the shared repository lacks it; the token reaches git only in its environment
  %%> Decided by the orchestrator, for review:
  %%> - the fetch is its own step, so that the build runs its script from the commit being released, not from the live release
  SW->>GN: Build the release<br/>wake and update preparation
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - refuses a commit that does not descend from the current release unless forced
  %%> - on a container Gateway, checks the target commit's activation workflow and recovery script before waking it or loading its Swamp workflows
  %%> - checks out the exact commit and installs dependencies in the preparation container; its workers and scheduler stay disabled
  %%> - a retry after an incomplete build starts from a clean checkout and discards partial build output
  %%> On failure:
  %%> - a new build refuses with `gateway.release_disk_low` before it writes, when the free space and the snapshots that may go cannot hold the build, a database copy and the floor
  SW->>GN: Install the web build<br/>artifact · digest · rename
  SW->>GN: Clone the prepared release<br/>seal · snapshot · copy
  SW->>GN: Snapshot the database<br/>VACUUM INTO
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - keeps the floor of Doctor's `node.disk_low`: 2 GiB and 10 % of the disk stay free after the copy
  %%> - removes older snapshots before the copy when the floor needs it; keeps the newest two after it, and always the one a pause names
  %%> On failure:
  %%> - refuses with `gateway.release_disk_low` before the copy; nothing migrated, the old release stays live
  SW->>GN: Sleep preparation<br/>parallel with candidate checks
  SW->>GN: Migrate<br/>artisan migrate --isolated
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - prints the end of the migration's output and its exit code; a failed exec would keep no output
  Note over SW: Check the migration<br/>assert the exit code
  %%> On failure:
  %%> - from here until the switch, the release pauses with the old release live
  %%> - the record's message ends with the migration's output
  SW->>GN: Wait for active Operations<br/>Gateway DB · at most 10 minutes
  %%> When:
  %%> - before Swamp load, while the old release and Horizon serve
  %%> - every 5 seconds while queued, running or waiting Operations covered by the [release idle guard](/reference/gateway-recovery#release-idle-guard) remain
  %%> Why:
  %%> - admitted execution input can still depend on the running Gateway code
  %%> On failure:
  %%> - refuses with `gateway.release_busy` and the blocking Operation IDs; the old release and Horizon stay live, and automatic releases pause because migrations ran
  alt Operations still active after 10 minutes
    SW--xGW: gateway.release_busy<br/>blocking Operation IDs
  else idle
    SW->>GN: Check the candidate<br/>FrankenPHP · health · commit
    %%> On failure:
    %%> - discard the candidate; live keeps serving and the Swamp load does not start
    Note over SW: Load Swamp on Node 209<br/>operation-gateway-swamp-load
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - the load child checks the target on the Gateway Node before updating the checkout, grants and loaded workflows
    Note over SW: Hand over the release<br/>gateway-release-activate
    %%> Why:
    %%> - the child runs from the definition the load installed, so the switch runs the new commit's steps
    opt the Gateway serves through host PHP-FPM
      AC->>GN: Drain Horizon<br/>systemctl stop · SIGTERM only
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - waits for the unit's whole control group to empty, up to the drain limit
      %%> On failure:
      %%> - the run fails with `gateway.release_horizon_unit_stale` for a unit without the stop policy, or `gateway.release_horizon_not_drained` when the unit did not stop in time
    end
    AC->>GN: Switch the release<br/>journal · drain · reload Caddy
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - for a container switch, save the active Horizon units under the release lock before stopping them, then point Caddy at the privately verified clone
    %%> - for a host PHP-FPM release, switch the links and reload PHP-FPM
    AC->>GN: Verify the Gateway<br/>/up · status version
    opt the check failed
      AC->>GN: Switch back<br/>restore · verify previous release
      %%> On failure:
      %%> - container recovery keeps its journal until the previous release passes through Caddy and its services are restored
    end
    AC->>GN: Start Horizon<br/>verified container or host PHP-FPM
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - after container verification, start Horizon on the new live release. A successful switch-back restores the previous release's workers
    %%> - on host PHP-FPM, start Horizon even after a failed drain or switch
    opt switch verified and Horizon started
      AC->>GN: Retire the previous live<br/>drain · freeze · reclaim to swap
      AC->>GN: Prune old releases<br/>remove displaced rollback
    end
    AC->>GN: Resume document cleanup<br/>after retirement or switch-back
    %%> Why:
    %%> - the scheduler restart paused the release cleanups; one that stays paused never fails the release
    alt every step succeeded
      SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal result
      Note over GW: Record verified<br/>fleet rollout follows
      %%> Next:
      %%> - the Gateway queues the existing fleet admission job; it follows each Node’s delivery and scoped role converge in order
      %%> - when enabled, nested-fleet refresh follows the first transition to `current`; with fleet rollout disabled it follows verification
    else a step before Migrate fails
      SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step
      Note over GW: Mark failed<br/>nothing changed · rerun safe
    else the check failed, switched back
      SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step
      Note over GW: Record switched back<br/>alert · next commit releases
    else another step from Migrate on fails
      SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step
      Note over GW: Pause automatic releases<br/>snapshot named · alert
    end
  end
  SW->>GN: Release unused candidate<br/>after handover or failure
  %%> Removes only an unpromoted clone owned by this Operation. Live and rollback remain protected.
  end
